---
import Websites from "../layouts/Websites.astro";

export const prerender = true;
---

<Websites
  title="Privacy policy · Lorenzo Marchisio"
  description="How lorenzomarchisio.me handles the data sent through its forms."
  back="/"
  skip={{ href: "#content", label: "Skip to content" }}
  jsonLd={[]}
>
  <article class="ws-section policy">
    <h1 class="ws-h2">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: 17 September 2026</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>Lorenzo Marchisio, reachable at <a href="mailto:me@lorenzomarchisio.me">me@lorenzomarchisio.me</a>.</p>

    <h2>What is collected</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Project request form</strong> (on the websites page): your name, email and business
      name, and, if you give them, your phone number and message. The form also sends the package
      you clicked on, if any, and, if you arrived from a link I sent, a short label for that link.
    </p>
    <p><strong>Contact form</strong> (on the home page): your name, email and message.</p>

    <h2>Why, and on what legal basis</h2>
    <p>
      To reply to you and, for a project request, to prepare a proposal. For project requests, the
      legal basis is taking steps at your request before a contract (GDPR, Article 6(1)(b)). For the
      contact form, it is my legitimate interest in replying to messages sent to me (Article
      6(1)(f)).
    </p>

    <h2>How long it is kept</h2>
    <p>
      Requests are kept for 12 months if no project starts, then deleted. If a project starts, they
      are kept for as long as the contract and accounting law require.
    </p>

    <h2>Who receives it</h2>
    <p>
      Form submissions are delivered to me by email only; nothing is stored in a database. These
      processors handle data on my behalf: <strong>Resend</strong> (email delivery), my email
      provider, and <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (hosting and delivery of this site). Resend and
      Cloudflare are based in the United States; those transfers rely on the EU–US Data Privacy
      Framework or the European Commission's standard contractual clauses. Your data is never sold
      or shared for advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and storage</h2>
    <p>This site sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask to access, correct or delete your data, to restrict or object to its use, or to
      receive it in a portable format. Email
      <a href="mailto:me@lorenzomarchisio.me">me@lorenzomarchisio.me</a>. You can also complain to a
      data protection authority, such as the Belgian Data Protection Authority or the one where you
      live.
    </p>
  </article>
</Websites>

<style>
  .policy {
    border-top: 0;
  }

  .policy > * {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .meta {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--warm);
  }

  .policy h2 {
    margin: 36px 0 10px;
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-stretch: 90%;
  }

  .policy p {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    color: var(--caption);
  }

  .policy a {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--signal);
  }
</style>
